  interkit - Debian + Fossil


  Welcome to interkit - a small Debian server with mail, chat, a relay and a web admin.

  FIRST: run the guided setup (it asks for your domain and walks you through everything):

        sudo interkit-setup

  New to Linux? The basics:
    ls                 list files                  cd FOLDER       go into a folder (cd .. = back)
    pwd                where am I                  cat FILE        show a file
    vim FILE / nano    edit a file (nano is easier; in vim quit with Esc then :q!)
    sudo COMMAND       run a command as administrator (asks for YOUR password; nothing shows while you type)
    ip -br a           show this machine's IP address (to connect from another computer: ssh USER@THAT-IP)
    htop               what is running (q to quit)      man COMMAND    manual for a command (q to quit)
    reboot / poweroff  restart / shut down (use sudo)   Tab key        completes names; Up arrow = previous command
  No copy/paste on this screen? Log in from your own computer with ssh and paste there.
  Help: interkit-setup -h
